Branching Strategies

There are three major strategies used in the industry.

1. GitHub Flow ⭐

Simple and widely used.

main
 │
 ├── feature-login
 │       │
 │       ▼
 │   Pull Request
 │
 ▼
Merge

Steps:

Create a feature branch.
Commit changes.
Push to GitHub.
Open a Pull Request.
Code review.
Merge into main.
CI/CD deploys.

Best for:

SaaS
Cloud-native applications
Continuous deployment
2. GitFlow

More structured.

main
 │
 ├── develop
 │      │
 │      ├── feature/*
 │      ├── release/*
 │      └── hotfix/*

Branches:

Branch	Purpose
main	Production
develop	Integration
feature	New features
release	Release preparation
hotfix	Urgent production fixes

Best for:

Large teams
Scheduled releases
3. Trunk-Based Development

Everything integrates into a single main branch frequently.

main
 │
 ├─ small feature
 ├─ small fix
 ├─ enhancement

Developers create short-lived branches and merge quickly.

Best for:

High-frequency deployments
CI/CD-heavy organizations
